    using the definition of $\delta$ in \eqref{eq:new-4} for the final equality.  Now \eqref{eq:new-2} follows by taking square roots.

The following estimates hold:
	\begin{equation}\label{eq:new-15}
		\max \{0, \gamma \tau(e_n) - \gamma \beta\} \leq \min \{\tau(q), \gamma \tau(e_n) \}, \quad \tau \in X^\omega.
	\end{equation}

o see this, note that the only non-trivial claim in \eqref{eq:new-15} is
	\begin{equation}\label{eq:new-16}
		\gamma \tau(e_n) - \gamma \beta \leq \tau(q), \quad \tau \in X^\omega.
	\end{equation}
	For the rest of this paragraph, let $\tau \in X^\omega$ be fixed.
	Using the second part of \eqref{eq:new-14}, 
